course: dictionary
lesson: 536
title: Athlete: one word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Athlete usually means a person who is good at sports and trains hard to take part in them. The clues around the word tell you which meaning fits.
explain: «Referees are athletes too, running about 10 to 12 km a match.» The words running and match are the clues. A referee is someone who takes part in sport, so the meaning is a person in sport.
explain: Be careful with «athlete's foot». The 's shows it belongs to a foot, and the clues itchy and skin tell you it is an infection between the toes, not a person.
fact: An athlete is a person who is good at sports and trains to take part in them.
fact: In the UK, an athlete can also be someone who competes in athletics, such as running, jumping and throwing.
fact: Phrases you may meet include top athlete, professional athlete and Olympic athlete.
fact: Athlete's foot is an itchy skin infection between the toes. It is not a person.
fact: «Athletes who are tested are responsible for anything in their body», so they check every medicine with a doctor or pharmacist.
exercise: «Referees are athletes too, running about 10 to 12 km a match.» In this sentence, what does athlete mean? | A type of shoe for running | A short, rude reply | *A person who takes part in sport, here a referee | An itchy skin infection
exercise: «With good control people with asthma can do all sports, and many top athletes have asthma.» What clue tells you athletes are people who do sport? | The word asthma on its own | The word warming | Nothing, it is only a guess | *The words do all sports
exercise: Sam says «athlete's foot» means a runner with sore feet. What is the correct meaning? | *An itchy skin infection between the toes | A fast runner who trains every day | A pair of running shoes | A person who checks medicines
test: Why do athletes check every medicine with a doctor or pharmacist? | Because athletes never get ill | *Because some cold medicines contain banned substances | Because doctors like to talk | Because medicine is expensive
test: What does a professional athlete do? | Teaches maths in school | Works at a petrol station | Looks after a sore foot | *Earns money from playing or competing in sport
exam: Jayden asks, «What is an athlete?» Which answer is best? | Someone who has itchy feet | *A person who is good at sports and trains to take part in them | A shoe used only for running | A kind of medicine
